## Step 3 — Replace HubShop layout with a real sell screen
### Edit scene: `res://ui/screens/HubShop.tscn`
Replace the current simple VBox UI with this structure (names matter for the script below):

**Node tree**
- `HubShop` (Control) script `HubShop.gd`
  - `BG` (ColorRect) anchors full
  - `Root` (MarginContainer) anchors full
    - `HBox` (HBoxContainer)
      - `Left` (PanelContainer)
        - `Margin` (MarginContainer)
          - `VBox` (VBoxContainer)
            - `Title` (Label)
            - `Info` (Label)
            - `Cart` (Label)
            - `Hover` (Label)
            - `ButtonsRow` (HBoxContainer)
              - `MarkAllBag` (Button)
              - `MarkNEG` (Button)
              - `Clear` (Button)
            - `IncludeEquipped` (CheckBox) text “Include Equipped”
            - `SellSelected` (Button) text “Sell Selected”
            - `Continue` (Button)
            - `Menu` (Button)
      - `Equipped` (PanelContainer)
        - `Margin` (MarginContainer)
          - `VBox` (VBoxContainer)
            - `EquippedTitle` (Label)
            - `InventoryBar` (instance `res://ui/components/InventoryBar.tscn`)
      - `Backpack` (PanelContainer)
        - `Margin` (MarginContainer)
          - `VBox` (VBoxContainer)
            - `BackpackTitle` (Label)
            - `BagGrid` (instance `res://ui/widgets/ShopBagGrid.tscn`)
  - `ConfirmSell` (ConfirmationDialog)

You can keep it visually simple (like your current UI style). The important part is node names/paths.

